\section{Notes}{

\code{pandoc_str()} holds a maximal run of non-whitespace characters: Pandoc
represents spaces as \link{pandoc_space} and line breaks as \link{pandoc_soft_break}
/ \link{pandoc_line_break}. Embedding ASCII whitespace in \verb{@text} would emit
literal whitespace that re-parses into separate inlines, so it is rejected.

\code{pandoc_shortcode()} carries \code{positional_args} and \code{keyword_args} as lists
of arg records. Each arg record is a list with \code{kind} ∈ \code{"string"},
\code{"number"}, \code{"boolean"}, \code{"shortcode"}, \code{"kv"}, \code{"kv_group"}.
\code{string}/\code{number}/\code{boolean} carry a \code{value}; \code{shortcode} carries a nested
\code{pandoc_shortcode} in \code{value}; \code{kv} carries \code{key} (character) and \code{value}
(another arg record); \code{kv_group} carries \code{value} as a list of \code{kv} records
(used for positional KeyValue bundles).
}

